"id":"euler.lemma-2.7","kind":"claim","label":"Lemma 2.7","locator":"Lemma 2.7, Section 2","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Lemma 2.7.** Assume (2.7), and let $\\mathbf a$ be the amplitude vector of Lemma 2.6. Put $E_{1,+}=k/|k|$, $E_{2,+}=\\mathbf a/|\\mathbf a|$ and $E_{3,+}=E_{1,+}\\times E_{2,+}$, and define $$\\nu_+=E_{1,+}\\cdot ME_{2,+},\\qquad\n \\eta_+=E_{3,+}\\cdot ME_{2,+}.$$ Then $\\nu_+\\ge\\varepsilon\\nu/2$ on $0\\le\\tau\\le T$. Where $\\varepsilon\\tan\\varphi\\ge1$, that is, for $\\sqrt2/\\varepsilon\\le\\tau\\le T$, $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left|\\frac{\\nu_+}{\\nu}-1\\right|\\le\\varepsilon,\\qquad\n \\left|\\frac{\\eta_+/\\nu_+}{\\cos\\varphi}-1\\right|\\le\\frac12. \\tag{2.19}\n\\end{equation}$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.7","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.7","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.4%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.4"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.lemma-2.7","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.5%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.lemma-2.7%22%2C%22euler.lemma-2.5%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_su